meta {
  name: Activities
}

auth {
  mode: inherit
}

docs {
  Event activities.

  Running this folder leaves two residues per run, both by design.

  One CANCELLED activity: the `draftActivityId` fixture has to serve the
  DRAFT, SCHEDULED and CANCELLED assertions, so a single activity walks the
  whole lifecycle and the retention rule forbids removing it afterwards. The
  API answers 409 and the trigger blocks the direct SQL delete, so this residue
  is unavoidable until there is an age-based purge or an administrative
  endpoint. `pnpm run prisma:cleanup:dev -- --pattern='Actividad temporal%'
  --apply` is the sanctioned way to clear it.

  One orphan speaker in the catalog: the full payload request links
  ana.prueba@utp.ac.pa, and deleting the activity unlinks the speaker but keeps
  the catalog entry, which is what the retention rule for the speakers catalog
  prescribes. The cleanup script deliberately does not remove catalog entries,
  so this one needs a manual delete.
}
